# Firebase configuration
#
# src/firebase.js was ignored from the first commit, back when it hardcoded the
# project's web API key. It is now a required source module — persistence.js,
# firestoreAdapter.js and the telemetry dashboard all import from it, and the
# build fails with MISSING_EXPORT without it — and it reads every value from
# VITE_FIREBASE_* instead of embedding anything. So it must be tracked.
#
# This rule is why the file kept "failing to commit": `git add src/firebase.js`
# was silently refused, and only the build on a clean clone revealed it.
# Do not re-add it. Secrets belong in .env, which is still ignored below.
.vercel

# Secrets (Firebase service-account JSON, .env)
.env
.env.local
secrets/
*service-account*.json

